<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
        Five stones in a row, centred in the adaptive-icon safe zone, and one katana cut
        across the whole row.

        The cut is drawn in three layers, in this order:
          1. the stones themselves;
          2. the slice — a 3.6-unit band painted in the colour of the background layer,
             so the row reads as cut through rather than merely crossed out;
          3. the edge of the blade — a thin glint inside the slice, 1.8 units at its
             widest and pointed at both ends, which is what makes the cut read as a
             sword instead of a line.

        The stroke is deliberately shallow (about 8°): at a steeper angle it would graze
        the outermost stones instead of cutting them, and the point is that all five are
        crossed out — five in a row is what ends the game.

        The band runs past the row into the margin the launcher mask crops; since it
        matches the background colour, that crop is invisible.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#1A1A1A"
        android:pathData="M30,54 m -7,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#1A1A1A"
        android:pathData="M42,54 m -7,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#1A1A1A"
        android:pathData="M54,54 m -7,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M66,54 m -7,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#1A1A1A"
        android:pathData="M78,54 m -7,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a 7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />

    <!-- The slice. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/ic_launcher_background"
        android:pathData="M12.66,61.6 L95.84,49.96 L95.34,46.4 L12.16,58.04 Z" />

    <!--
        The blade's edge. Its points stop just short of the visible edge of the mask,
        otherwise a round launcher would crop them and the cut would lose its tips.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#EAF4FF"
        android:pathData="M20.33,58.71 L37.27,57.15 L54.12,54.89 L71.95,52.43 L87.67,49.29 L71.73,50.85 L53.88,53.11 L37.05,55.57 Z" />
</vector>
